    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Mental health remains a taboo topic in many societies in Africa and many victims choose to suffer in silence rather than seeking the support they need. In the wake of the Rwandan genocide's 25th anniversary, the topic of mental health continues to gain importance as the concern around intergenerational trauma grows.",
